{
  "annotations": {
    "list": []
  },
  "editable": true,
  "fiscalYearStartMonth": 0,
  "graphTooltip": 1,
  "id": null,
  "links": [],
  "panels": [
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "description": "Question answered: Which sensor or subsystem stopped agreeing, and when?\n\nHow to read it: A single hot row points to one diverging source. Many hot rows can mean real scene change, estimator issue, synchronization problem, or global telemetry issue.\n\nWhy it matters: Robotics engineers debug by source such as lidar, camera, IMU, wheel encoders, odometry, localization, controller, and actuator.\n\nNext action: If one row is hot, inspect that source. If many rows are hot, inspect estimator, clock sync, environment event, or mission transition.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "yellow",
                "value": 20
              },
              {
                "color": "orange",
                "value": 50
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 75
              }
            ]
          },
          "unit": "percent"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "max by (source, subsystem) (metricchrono_robot_source_disagreement_score{site=\"$site\",environment=\"$environment\",recipe=\"robotics-telemetry\",asset_group=~\"$asset_group\",asset=~\"$asset\",source=~\"$source\",comparison=~\"source_vs_source|sensor_vs_estimator\"})",
          "legendFormat": "{{source}} {{subsystem}}",
          "range": true,
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Source Agreement Heatmap",
      "type": "heatmap"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "description": "Question answered: Which source is currently least trustworthy?\n\nHow to read it: Low score means the source has repeatedly disagreed, gone missing, or become stale. It is a triage hint, not a permanent calibration judgment.\n\nWhy it matters: Engineers need a prioritized sensor list during incidents.\n\nNext action: Inspect the lowest-trust source's driver status, timestamps, physical condition, and mounting.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "orange",
                "value": 50
              },
              {
                "color": "yellow",
                "value": 80
              },
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": 90
              }
            ]
          },
          "unit": "percent"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 0
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "min by (source) (min_over_time(metricchrono_robot_source_reliability_score{site=\"$site\",environment=\"$environment\",recipe=\"robotics-telemetry\",asset_group=~\"$asset_group\",asset=~\"$asset\",source=~\"$source\"}[2m]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{source}} reliability",
          "range": true,
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Source Reliability / Trust Score",
      "type": "stat"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "description": "Question answered: Is the robot losing localization or just moving differently?\n\nHow to read it: Localization disagreement with stable actuator tracking points toward estimator or perception. Tracking deviation with stable localization points toward control or actuation.\n\nWhy it matters: This separates the robot not knowing where it is from the robot not executing what it wants.\n\nNext action: Inspect map, feature quality, lidar/camera health, IMU calibration, wheel slip, and covariance.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "yellow",
                "value": 20
              },
              {
                "color": "orange",
                "value": 50
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 75
              }
            ]
          },
          "unit": "percent"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 8
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "metricchrono_robot_localization_disagreement_score{site=\"$site\",environment=\"$environment\",recipe=\"robotics-telemetry\",asset_group=~\"$asset_group\",asset=~\"$asset\",comparison=\"sensor_vs_estimator\"}",
          "legendFormat": "{{asset}} localization",
          "range": true,
          "refId": "A"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "metricchrono_robot_odometry_disagreement_score{site=\"$site\",environment=\"$environment\",recipe=\"robotics-telemetry\",asset_group=~\"$asset_group\",asset=~\"$asset\",comparison=\"source_vs_source\"}",
          "legendFormat": "{{asset}} odometry",
          "range": true,
          "refId": "B"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "metricchrono_robot_imu_disagreement_score{site=\"$site\",environment=\"$environment\",recipe=\"robotics-telemetry\",asset_group=~\"$asset_group\",asset=~\"$asset\",comparison=\"source_vs_source\"}",
          "legendFormat": "{{asset}} IMU",
          "range": true,
          "refId": "C"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Odometry / Localization / IMU Agreement",
      "type": "timeseries"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "description": "Question answered: Did the robot's perception input change even though the mission state did not?\n\nHow to read it: Rising perception change with normal motion can indicate occlusion, lighting change, dust, scene change, feature loss, or camera/lidar degradation.\n\nWhy it matters: Perception problems often present as downstream navigation or control anomalies.\n\nNext action: Inspect camera/lidar status, lighting, occlusion, lens or sensor cleanliness, and environment.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "yellow",
                "value": 20
              },
              {
                "color": "orange",
                "value": 50
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 75
              }
            ]
          },
          "unit": "percent"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 8
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "metricchrono_robot_perception_change_score{site=\"$site\",environment=\"$environment\",recipe=\"robotics-telemetry\",asset_group=~\"$asset_group\",asset=~\"$asset\",comparison=\"known_good_baseline\"}",
          "legendFormat": "{{asset}} perception",
          "range": true,
          "refId": "A"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "metricchrono_robot_feature_count_change_score{site=\"$site\",environment=\"$environment\",recipe=\"robotics-telemetry\",asset_group=~\"$asset_group\",asset=~\"$asset\",comparison=\"sensor_vs_estimator\"}",
          "legendFormat": "{{asset}} feature count change",
          "range": true,
